1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,120
Sorry, follow!

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,580
I'm really amazed that you set a ball from that low.

3
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,220
You could just go underhanded.

4
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:24,820
Oh, no, I couldn't, because it is my job to set.

5
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,780
I'm responsible for getting the ball to the best spot.

6
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:28,860
So?

7
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:32,280
So, underhand, I only have my two arms.

8
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,640
Overhand, I've got ten fingers.

9
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:38,040
I want the most contact points to get better support.

10
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,780
Because I'm a setter!

11
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:45,500
I'm on a team with someone who plays volleyball like that.

12
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:49,200
I've been half-assing everything so much.

13
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:56,460
Rusecki, we don't need you to just get the ball over the net.

14
00:00:56,460 --> 00:01:01,240
I was almost certain I'd never get another chance.

15
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:07,280
Even the best team in the world can't keep doing exactly the same things, or they'll find

16
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:09,080
themselves knocked off their top spot.

17
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:09,960
Huh?

18
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:12,300
And we aren't even the best team in Japan.

19
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:13,460
Not yet.

20
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:16,680
If yesterday satisfies us, what happens tomorrow?

21
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,400
Opportunities are out there, son.

22
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,480
You have to challenge yourself today.

23
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,320
You have to challenge yourself today.

24
00:01:31,320 --> 00:02:01,300
We'll be right back.

25
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:31,300
We'll be right back.

26
00:02:31,320 --> 00:03:01,300
We'll be right back.

27
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:04,060
Nice serve!

28
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:07,280
Opportunities are out there, son.

29
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:09,360
You have to challenge yourself today.

30
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,680
Nice serve, Riseki!

31
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,540
Nice serve, Riseki!

32
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:22,040
In a complete 180 from the second set, Riseki lets loose a tremendous serve!

33
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:22,680
Yes! Yes!

34
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:23,120
Yes!

35
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:25,120
That's what I'm talking about!

36
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:30,420
This guy's manageable, let's shut him down right now.

37
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:31,340
Yes, sir!

38
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:37,600
So basically every person in Inarizaki's cheer squad is like that old guy with the mutton chops.

39
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:40,720
If they think a play is good, they cheer.

40
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,220
If not, they boo.

41
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:49,620
After a quick timeout, it's Riseki's turn to serve again.

42
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,240
Can he keep his concentration?

43
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:57,360
Tanaka!

44
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:00,280
It's long!

45
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:07,840
Threw them off with a serve and then Alan Ojiro nails it!

46
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:08,660
All right!

47
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:10,300
That was masterfully done!

48
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:10,880
Nice!

49
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,460
Nice kill, Alan!

50
00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:14,060
Jump, jump, Alan!

51
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:17,740
And just like that, Inarizaki has caught up to Karasuno!

52
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,820
Don't panic, you guys!

53
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:20,720
We're fine.

54
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:21,560
We're fine.

55
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:40,420
Hey, nice job, dude.

56
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:42,500
I'll get three points next time.

57
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:44,300
You gotta dream bigger than three points.

58
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,180
Ten at least.

59
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:56,160
One hundred percent.

60
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:56,240
One hundred percent.

61
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:12,840
Gene!

62
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:14,800
He's really coming for him now.

63
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:15,940
Nice serve!

64
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:27,720
Kageyama!

65
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:28,700
Left!

66
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:29,220
Tanaka!

67
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:34,760
Number five on the left has a brutal cut shot.

68
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:35,780
But...

69
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,380
It's just a cheap imitation.

70
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:48,060
You're nothing but a bad copy of Bokuto.

71
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:50,240
And it's blocked!

72
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:53,820
Tanaka's been on a roll ever since the end of the first set.

73
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:56,040
But now they've stopped him in his tracks.

74
00:05:56,420 --> 00:06:01,080
Looks like third-year-o Mimi has finally filled up the hole in Inarizaki's defense.

75
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:04,360
Inarizaki didn't only find a way to catch up.

76
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:08,100
With that run, they managed to turn things around and take the lead.

77
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:13,160
With 13 points, Inarizaki is well on their way to getting this game under control.

78
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:16,220
Now at the midway point, the teams will change sides.

79
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:22,100
It would seem that the serves from first-year Rizeki have turbocharged Inarizaki.

80
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,940
They're really picking up steam now.

81
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:26,740
Aggressive serves are a powerful standalone weapon.

82
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:32,420
They can put pressure on the opposition while simultaneously galvanizing the server's own team.

83
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:36,060
Of course, it's not as easy as it looks.

84
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:39,160
Will Karasuno be able to stop Inarizaki's momentum?

85
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:41,920
Inarizaki is still showing some instability.

86
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:47,280
Each team member is a skilled player, but they don't always work well together.

87
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:50,100
And their aggression can sometimes backfire on them.

88
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:52,820
But the opposite is also true.

89
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:55,220
And that's why they call them the ultimate challengers.

90
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:58,640
The fact that they ranked second in the country is proof of that.

91
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:02,940
It's gonna get rough if they don't end the streak right here and now.

92
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:05,400
Who the hell cares about being second in Japan?

93
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:06,320
Second?

94
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:07,560
Or third?

95
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:09,640
And it doesn't really matter.

96
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,580
That was yesterday.

97
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:15,960
Cover!

98
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:18,520
Yesterday is already digested.

99
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:19,980
Finish it, Kageyama!

100
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:23,580
Lots of yesterdays have already been converted into muscle.

101
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:30,160
That was a difficult shot, but Kageyama got it back over and right at center of Tsumumiya!

102
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:30,780
Asamu!

103
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:34,940
But Inarizaki still has...

104
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:36,180
Osamumiya!

105
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,820
The number two over the center.

106
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,800
Or the ace on the left side.

107
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:46,380
What are we gonna do today?

108
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,840
Twin quick minus tempo!

109
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:52,560
Reverse!

110
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:52,620
Reverse!

111
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:06,200
What just happened?

112
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:08,540
Nice kill at Tsumumu!

113
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:10,200
Nice kill at Tsumumu!

114
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:11,820
Drop, drop at Tsumumu!

115
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:12,280
Whoa!

116
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:13,780
Unbelievable!

117
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,480
The spiker sets the ball to the center!

118
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:20,760
And together they deliver a stunning minus tempo quick attack!

119
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:24,200
The Mia twins are a force to be reckoned with, Bill!

120
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:28,480
If yesterday satisfies us, what happens tomorrow?

121
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:35,180
What the hell?

122
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:35,780
Damn!

123
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:38,740
Yeah!

124
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:41,680
But just so you know, it was too low on a bit short.

125
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:43,680
You just can't be choosers, you ungrateful jerk!

126
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:44,520
I'm not a true center!

127
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:47,320
But if we tried, I bet we could land a Skylove hurricane now!

128
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,120
Sure, fun!

129
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,400
You're on bottom!

130
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:49,700
What?

131
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:51,040
We both know you're on bottom!

132
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:51,940
That was a fluke!

133
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,180
Don't let it get to you!

134
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:53,720
Nope!

135
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:54,020
Right!

136
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:58,780
Even if it was a fluke, it's still bound to shake the other team's confidence some.

137
00:08:59,040 --> 00:08:59,800
Bet you're right.

138
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:04,380
That must feel awful.

139
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:07,080
First, we take the lead away.

140
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:09,360
Then we hit you with a move you didn't see coming.

141
00:09:09,780 --> 00:09:10,760
Anyone will be panicking.

142
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:13,300
I bet you want to get out of this funk.

143
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:20,020
At times like this, pulling off a spectacular kill would clear the air instantly and improve

144
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:20,800
your team's morale.

145
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:24,920
You want to get that spike over even if it kills you.

146
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:28,300
But even if it kills us...

147
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:33,080
We'll stop it.

148
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:36,300
And he's shut down!

149
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:40,760
Inanazaki has stopped Karasuno's ace, Azumari Asahi!

150
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,300
I think that if this keeps up...

151
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:45,100
Karasuno is going to lose.

152
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,600
I hit the last one way too hard!

153
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:50,120
I'm sorry!

154
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:51,360
Probably because you're...

155
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,420
Guess he touched the net.

156
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:53,020
Shut the trap!

157
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:53,320
That's lucky.

158
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:57,500
But the mental beating that's happening is still far worse for Karasuno.

159
00:09:58,020 --> 00:09:59,020
Now we can catch up.

160
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:02,620
Dammit.

161
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:07,300
I've been managing to block out Inanazaki's cheer squad, but it feels like they're closing

162
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:08,000
in again.

163
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,540
Get out there, Hinata!

164
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:14,260
And now Karasuno's bringing middle blocker Hinata up to the front.

165
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:19,600
This kid is not only an excellent scorer, but one of the best decoys we'll see in this

166
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:19,940
tournament.

167
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:22,100
Karasuno's trying to tie this thing up.

168
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:22,780
Please, Hinata.

169
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:23,960
I'm backing you.

170
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:25,540
You gotta do something.

171
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:29,920
Asahi!

172
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:32,620
It's up!

173
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:33,000
Hinata!

174
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:33,020
Hinata!

175
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:40,300
And Inanazaki lost control of the ball, but...

176
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:42,560
Ojiro fires off a powerful smash!

177
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:43,400
Hinata!

178
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:59,660
It seems to me Inanazaki's blocks are just getting more and more accurate.

179
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:00,720
Kageyama.

180
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:01,320
Hmm?

181
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,400
It hurts to ask you to do this, but...

182
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:05,800
Hinata!

183
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:09,660
Yes!

184
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:10,140
Yes!

185
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:10,820
Nice kill!

186
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:11,500
Nice kill!

187
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:13,340
And now Kageyama's up to serve.

188
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:13,700
Go for it, Kageyama!

189
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:16,240
Karasuno is really going to need those breakpoints.

190
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,120
Number nine has a powerful serve.

191
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:23,520
And they've got three attackers up front, including number ten.

192
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,620
That's their most dangerous rotation.

193
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:32,420
Chance ball!

194
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:32,920
Oh!

195
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,720
Ugh, I hate this rotation.

196
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:42,140
You're not getting breakpoint!

197
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:44,460
Nice receive!

198
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:45,920
Crap, it's long!

199
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:49,220
I'm done.

200
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:49,340
I'm done.

201
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,380
I'm gonna stop him!

202
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:56,540
Yes!

203
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:02,960
Hang on!

204
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:04,840
What's the other team getting that point for?

205
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:05,860
It was a reachover.

206
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:06,500
Huh?

207
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:10,720
Hinata and Tanaka probably thought they were blocking Asumu's dump.

208
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,420
But instead, he was actually about to do a set.

209
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:19,200
Ultimately, it's against the rules to touch the ball when it's still in the other team's court.

210
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:20,940
Son of a bitch.

211
00:12:21,140 --> 00:12:22,640
You baited him into doing that.

212
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:28,220
We both know that the one who dominates the net isn't the big tall guy or the middle blockers.

213
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:30,380
It's the one whose turf is the net.

214
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:31,640
The setter.

215
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:43,440
And now the rotation brings back Hinata Zaki's most powerful server, Asumu Miya.

216
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:50,980
We'll see if Karasuno can survive another Asumu onslaught.

217
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:51,980
Whoa!

218
00:12:51,980 --> 00:13:05,320
That ball went directly back into Hinata Zaki's court!

219
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:08,040
Karasuno does survive a bit longer, Phil.

220
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:12,060
Seems like Karasuno is just barely hanging on down there.

221
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:12,860
Yeah.

222
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,080
Tsukishima?

223
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:17,980
Kick some ass out there!

224
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:19,800
Dammit.

225
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:24,400
Now there's setters in the back, so they're all in position to use the twins quick again.

226
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:25,940
Block them, guys.

227
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:26,540
Please!

228
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:33,220
That receive goes back to the center.

229
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,360
Who will Asumu Miya use?

230
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:41,180
The attack comes from the left with Hitoshi Kijima!

231
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:43,660
Hell yeah!

232
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:47,380
But Karasuno's premier blocker Tsukishima stands in his way!

233
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:48,120
One more time!

234
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:49,400
Man, I got it!

235
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:50,020
Usamu!

236
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:50,420
Huh?

237
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:57,720
Asumu Miya once again turns first contact directly into a set!

238
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,260
You're not Tsukishima.

239
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:04,680
Tsukishima is on point today.

240
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:07,460
Osamu Miya is waiting to slam it down!

241
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:13,940
What?

242
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:18,080
The ball is set to Asumu Miya, and he sets it right back!

243
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:21,600
Karasuno's blockers are totally left in the cold!

244
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,020
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

245
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:24,580
Dammit.

246
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:28,500
And coming from behind, it's Alan Ojudo!

247
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:28,900
Oh!

248
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:31,580
Ugh!

249
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:46,420
Ah!

250
00:14:46,420 --> 00:15:03,540
Impressive.

251
00:15:04,540 --> 00:15:08,660
After a long stretch of time that likely had seen more than its share of adversity.

252
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:11,840
Very rarely do you see something like this.

253
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:15,460
A play that gets your heart racing just thinking about it.

254
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:18,840
A play that revives your lost confidence.

255
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:26,500
After a long, strenuous climb to the top, it serves as the foothold you so desperately need.

256
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:28,620
It's not a miracle.

257
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:32,980
It may be one play out of a hundred, or even out of a thousand.

258
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:36,160
But it's something you went and took for yourself.

259
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:43,640
When you take hold and connect these rare moments, they allow you to climb higher and higher.

260
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:49,260
I never thought the day would come when I'd say this to you, but...

261
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:50,560
Nice receive.

262
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:57,800
They'll see you from the top.

263
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:01,420
But hey, you don't have to be in such a hurry.

264
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:05,580
Meanwhile, don't underestimate your new job.

265
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:11,360
Without the play of your personal setter, Kageyama, I don't see you as being worth anything.

266
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:15,940
He who climbs the ladder must start out at the bottom.

267
00:16:15,940 --> 00:16:20,560
What are you trying to accomplish?

268
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:20,780
What are you trying to accomplish?

269
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:47,700
Set, it's a bit low.

270
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,240
He's struggling with his approach.

271
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:52,480
A blocker straight ahead of him.

272
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:09,280
Even without their Yubaro, Kareseo kills that intense attack perfectly.

273
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:11,860
Courtesy of middle blocker Shouyo Hidata.

274
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:14,860
The kid's a real treat to watch.

275
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:15,920
A nice receiver.

276
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:16,800
Is that a fluke?

277
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:18,780
I mean, I guess you could call it that.

278
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:22,940
But they can't always be just luck, even if they are flukes.

279
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:23,740
Hmm.

280
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:25,820
I don't know what to call it.

281
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:30,680
But there was definitely a concentrated intent behind his actions.

282
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:40,200
The instant he made contact with the ball, he absorbed its force, using his whole body to kill its speed.

283
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:42,080
That slow spin.

284
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:43,220
It's perfect.

285
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:45,260
No, I'm not going to say it.

286
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:46,460
I'm not saying it yet.

287
00:17:47,420 --> 00:17:47,900
Counter!

288
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:49,260
Let's go!

289
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:50,420
Breakpoint time!

290
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:54,060
Synchronized attack!

291
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:55,640
Everyone!

292
00:17:56,920 --> 00:18:00,180
It's just one point, but it's one we cannot let them have.

293
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:03,440
The mood of the game has changed, and I don't like it.

294
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:05,020
Stop them!

295
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:06,900
Follow!

296
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:10,900
Follow!

297
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,260
Three blockers!

298
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,140
Great job, guys!

299
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:20,820
Nice wipe!

300
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:26,340
What the damn he's fast?

301
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:50,460
It's still in the air!

302
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:52,180
Can Anazaki send it back?

303
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:53,440
Yes!

304
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:53,560
Yes!

305
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:53,840
Yes!

306
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:54,380
Breakback!

307
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:55,580
One more time!

308
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:00,640
You've got to be kidding me.

309
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,020
No!

310
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:14,020
It wasn't a breakpoint.

311
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,220
It didn't even get us to matchpoint.

312
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:21,520
But even so, that single point was more than enough to shatter their spirits.

313
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:27,620
And once their spirits are broken, their bodies suddenly remember all the exhaustion that's

314
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:28,520
been building up.

315
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:30,820
Now, Specs.

316
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:36,740
That really showed phenomenal persistence on both sides.

317
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:40,400
But does Anazaki still draw the smile of the goddess of victory?

318
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:45,960
Anazaki scraped by there, and Karasano put it all into those two attacks.

319
00:19:46,040 --> 00:19:47,340
It must have hurt to get stopped.

320
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:48,580
That was so close.

321
00:19:48,760 --> 00:19:49,040
Yeah.

322
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:55,760
I don't want to lose.

323
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:57,440
I won't let them beat us.

324
00:19:57,580 --> 00:19:59,580
I'm not going to let this end.

325
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:00,620
We're not gonna...

326
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:01,280
Did you see that?

327
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:04,060
Did you see my receive just now?

328
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:14,220
Missed it.

329
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:15,520
You're a liar!

330
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:18,060
I heard you say nice receive!

331
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,100
I heard you!

332
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:20,280
That's okay.

333
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,940
Just make sure and watch me get the next one!

334
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:27,280
It's so hard sometimes.

335
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:29,380
That you just want to stop.

336
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:31,640
But you can't.

337
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:33,040
You have to get over it.

338
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:35,180
We're only at the first step.

339
00:20:35,180 --> 00:20:52,920
It's like he's having a good meal.

340
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:53,400
Huh?

341
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:54,980
Okay, seriously.

342
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:58,080
What is it about this match that's making you think so much about food?

343
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:02,900
You know how you eat too much yakiniku or whatever and make yourself sick?

344
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:05,360
So you figure you've had enough to last your whole life.

345
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:07,160
Then you want some the very next day?

346
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:11,140
No, if I've just had yakiniku, I'd rather have curry or sushi.

347
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:14,060
Each of us eats several times every day.

348
00:21:14,300 --> 00:21:15,500
Then we get hungry again.

349
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:18,380
And it always makes us happy whenever we get food.

350
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:20,480
It happens again and again.

351
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:23,180
But it still makes us just as happy every single time.

352
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:24,740
Oh yeah.

353
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:27,440
You do always look happy to be alive when you're eaten.

354
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:28,660
No matter what's in front of you.

355
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:32,180
Even if you're having cold rice balls or soggy ramen.

356
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:34,700
That's how it is.

357
00:21:35,180 --> 00:21:35,880
For that guy.

358
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:37,140
Hmm.

359
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,540
He plays volleyball.

360
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:42,740
Like he'd starve without it.

361
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:47,380
I mean, you know.

362
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:51,240
If you have a bite of something and you're starving.

363
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:56,760
It makes you even hungrier.

364
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:00,140
Yeah, I get what you're saying.

365
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:08,360
When they see someone enjoying their food that much.

366
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:19,000
Everyone else gets hungry too.

367
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:25,720
確かなことはいつか

368
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:28,560
分かる時が来るから

369
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:31,060
間違ったっていいさ

370
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:35,280
今思いを止めないで

371
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:37,260
バカマダムが

372
00:22:37,260 --> 00:22:37,680
ゼルト

373
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,800
Stan

374
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:41,660
ラー

375
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:47,220
イチュラー

376
00:22:47,220 --> 00:22:51,340
エチュラー

377
00:22:51,340 --> 00:22:52,620
スクービス

378
00:22:52,620 --> 00:22:52,960
目

379
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:54,960
パコ

380
00:22:54,960 --> 00:23:24,940
Thank you.

381
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:54,940
Thank you.

382
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:56,960
Thank you.

